    "basis": "A 35 mm tall bar with a glazed bottle, separately measured collar/stopper, two deep small bowls, a thin open timber frame, twelve fastening heads and hidden shelf ware. Independent 82000/28000 triangle meshes and 1024/512 bakes preserve vessel rims, rounded stopper, carved braces and fastening masks. Compare compact maps and inspect every fastening in LOD."
  },
  "reviewNotes": "PDF page 8 and native front/back/top inspected. Source 460010 triangles, 23000584 bytes, maximum height 68.823898 mm. A clear full-height centre ray reaches floor 24.706627 mm, normal Z=.991603; native mount datum 17 mm. Floor normal squares X=.377702, Y=.040437 confirm Y boards. Source components above Z43.55 separate two bowls, the frame and a bottle: the bowls centre near [-13.842,-7.203] and [-7.435,-3.349], with actual floors at Z43.665142 and 43.654495 mm. Their rims reach 46.322899 and 46.260300 mm. Bottle bounds X[-17.1265,-8.3207], Y[3.53065,12.33455], Z43.55..53.946297. Native neck profiles show a narrow neck through Z51.5, a wide collar Z51.5..52.75 and a rounded stopper above Z52.75, centred near X=-12.79,Y=7.98. The collar/stopper use independent pigments and roughness. Common timber compared against MT1-047: 662 source samples, median .004800 mm, P95 .010753, maximum .036306; .08 mm source matching preserves wood at contacts. Packed surfaces project back to MT1-048 before comparison. Four countertop heads and eight upper-frame heads were independently measured; cap centres use the first .025 mm of each protrusion. Braces use this source own edge probes, while the crossbeam and continuous uprights keep Y/Z grain. Check front/back/top, bottle/collar/stopper, both empty bowl floors, hidden shelf, all twelve fastening masks, unobstructed frame points away from the new bottle, both tiers and candidates before publication.",
